hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22695","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mount has perished, so carry me. He said: So he said: I have nothing. He said: Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not guide him to one who will carry him? He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever guides to good, for him is the like of the reward of its doer."
